# EBS Git Workflow Rules

Before committing:

1. inspect git status
2. identify intended files
3. exclude unrelated changes
4. exclude temporary QA artifacts
5. exclude secrets
6. verify build/lint/TypeScript/tests as appropriate

Do not commit:

- .env.local
- secrets
- API keys
- temporary screenshots
- .sprint-qa/
- debug artifacts
- unrelated documentation

Prefer scoped commits.

Commit-message style:

feat: <product change>
fix: <bug or correction>
refactor: <non-behavior structural change>
test: <test-only change>
docs: <documentation-only change>

Do not commit automatically after implementation unless the user explicitly approves the result.

When asked to commit:

- stage only the intended files
- commit with the approved message
- do not push
- report the commit hash
- report files committed
- report files excluded
- report whether the working tree is clean
- report remaining untracked files

Do not push unless the user explicitly asks to push.

Never assume that commit implies push.

When asked to commit and push:

- stage only the intended files
- commit with the approved message
- push to origin/main or the requested branch
- report the commit hash
- report files committed
- report files excluded
- report whether the working tree is clean
- report remaining untracked files

When asked only to push:

- push the current approved commit and branch as appropriate
- do not create a new commit
